From cf35022b5757b4fb32168984c9ef38785f802fc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Dowell <mbd06b+github@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:43:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/12] fix: a closed reader ends only read-only commands
 quietly, by error kind

Narrows 7786c8185 (review A2). It accepted any error whose chain or
message text ended in "Broken pipe (os error 32)", so a `push --porcelain`
whose reader closed mid-report exited 141 instead of its rejection, and a
failed read of a file whose name ends in that text was swallowed.

- `shared::closed_reader::Watch` wraps stdout and stderr in
  `prepare_and_run` and for `--cli-surface-json`, and records a write that
  failed with `ErrorKind::BrokenPipe`. Message text is never consulted.
- brit-cli `exit_status()` is now the one place the exit status is
  decided: 141 only when the command is in `READ_ONLY_COMMANDS` and a
  watched write saw the closed reader; a Git-shaped `Exit` keeps its
  status; everything else is reported with its own status.
- With global `-v`, an operation's own error wins over a failure to forward
  its buffered output.
- Journey: a reader that takes one line and closes during a large
  `branch list` / `for-each-ref` listing ends them with 141 and no report.
  Unit tests: an error merely containing the text is reported, and a
  mutating command's outcome is reported although its reader closed.

